<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ============================================================
    ic_video — video camera glyph (attach menu, video bubble badge)
    ------------------------------------------------------------
    Referenced by:
      - bottom_sheet_attach.xml (option_video leading icon)
      - future: video message bubble type badge (Phase 7)
      - future: video playback overlay play icon (Phase 7)

    Constraints this file honors:

    1. MONOCHROME TEMPLATE.
       Single fill color (#FFFFFFFF), tinted at the consumer
       level (app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurface" in
       bottom_sheet_attach.xml). Do NOT set a brand color
       here — the fill is a template.

    2. 24dp VIEWPORT.
       Matches every other chrome icon in the app. The attach
       sheet renders it at 24dp; future video overlays may
       render it larger (up to 48dp) — the vector scales
       losslessly.

    3. STANDARD MATERIAL "VIDEOCAM" GLYPH.
       This is Google's canonical Material Design "videocam"
       icon: a rectangular camera body on the left with a
       triangular "lens protrusion" pointing right. It is
       NOT a custom design. The entire world uses this shape
       for "video camera" and any deviation would read as a
       rendering error.

    4. SOLID FILL, NOT OUTLINED.
       The icon is a single solid shape (camera body + lens
       triangle merged). This matches the "image" icon next
       to it in the attach sheet (both solid, both filled).
       Mixing solid and outlined icons in the same option row
       would look visually inconsistent — the sheet uses all
       solid glyphs for its five icons.

    5. SINGLE PATH.
       The camera body and lens triangle are drawn as a
       single closed path — the triangle is attached to the
       body's right edge with no gap, producing one solid
       silhouette. This is the standard Material construction.
       Do NOT split into two paths (body + triangle) — that
       would produce a visible seam where they meet, and the
       two subpaths would not merge into a single recognizable
       "camera" silhouette.

    6. NO androidx.AutoMirrored.
       The videocam glyph is horizontally directional (the
       lens points right). Under RTL, mirroring would flip
       the lens to point left — but this is the standard
       convention (Video cameras point in the reading
       direction on RTL OS's — Instagram, WhatsApp, and every
       other Material app do NOT mirror their videocam icons
       because the "camera body on the left, lens on the
       right" convention is universal across both LTR and RTL
       users). Do not add auto-mirroring.

    Rendering result at 24dp:
      A solid camera body with a triangular lens pointing
      right — instant recognition as "video / record a video."
    ============================================================
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">

    <!--
        Canonical Material Design "videocam" path.

        Breakdown:
          M 17,10.5           top-right of the camera body
          V 7                 up the right edge
          c0,-1.1 -0.9,-2 -2,-2   top-right corner curve
          H 4                 left across the top edge
          c-1.1,0 -2,0.9 -2,2     top-left corner curve
          v 10                down the left edge
          c0,1.1 0.9,2 2,2        bottom-left corner curve
          h 11                right across the bottom edge
          c1.1,0 2,-0.9 2,-2      bottom-right corner curve
          v -3.5              up a bit (start of the
                              notch where the lens triangle
                              connects)
          l 5,4               diagonal line down-right
                              to the lens tip
          V 6                 straight up to the top of
                              the lens tip
          l -5,4.5            diagonal line back up-left
                              to rejoin the body
          z                   close

        Rendered result: a rounded-rectangle camera body
        with a triangular lens protrusion on the right side,
        connected at the body's upper-right and lower-right
        — the standard "video camera" silhouette.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M17,10.5V7c0,-1.1 -0.9,-2 -2,-2H4c-1.1,0 -2,0.9 -2,2v10c0,1.1 0.9,2 2,2h11c1.1,0 2,-0.9 2,-2v-3.5l5,4v-11l-5,4z" />

</vector>
